-- CK-101: a receiver on a cycle that passes through two method boundaries —
-- `A`'s `eq` asks its payload for `compare`, `B`'s `compare` asks its payload
-- for `eq` — is ONE `infinite_type` at the comparison, written as its
-- structure (checker-v2.md §9.5: the derivability verdict is one iterative
-- walk over `(node, method)` pairs, coloured per pair, so the cycle is met
-- whichever method the boundaries alternate through; §8.2, CK-57). On
-- 68186fa v1's `walkDerivable` recurses once per boundary and overflows the
-- stack; R6a's first round did the same (review B2, probe `cyc/`).
import Pa exposing (A)
import Pb exposing (B)


f x =
    if List.isEmpty [ x, A (B x) ] then
        ( x, 1 ) == ( x, 1 )

    else
        False
